        "passed": true,
        "reason": "TypeScript code is well-structured with correct imports, types, and module references. Minor concern: `response._response.status` in deleteBlob uses a semi-internal property, but it is still present in @azure/storage-blob v12 types. Code should compile."
      },
      {
        "name": "Latest Package Versions",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "All Azure SDK packages match latest: @azure/storage-blob 12.31.0, @azure/identity 4.13.1, @azure/logger 1.3.0."
      },
      {
        "name": "Best Practices",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses ManagedIdentityCredential for production, async/await throughout, streaming uploads, lease-based concurrency control, proper cleanup in finally blocks."
      },
      {
        "name": "Error Handling",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "No specific error handling anywhere. No RestError catches, no status-code-based branching for 404/409. Only a generic .catch() on the top-level main()."
      },
      {
        "name": "Code Quality",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Clean, well-typed TypeScript. Good separation of concerns (config, service, main). Proper interfaces for options and results. Sensible defaults with env-var overrides."
      },
      {
        "name": "Correct @azure/ Scoped Packages",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "All dependencies use @azure/ scoped packages: @azure/storage-blob, @azure/identity, @azure/logger."
      },
      {
        "name": "@azure/identity for Authentication",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses ManagedIdentityCredential from @azure/identity. No connection strings, account keys, or SAS tokens in code."
      },
      {
        "name": "Client Constructor with Endpoint and Credential",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "BlobServiceClient constructed with endpoint URL and credential: new BlobServiceClient(config.accountEndpoint, credential, options)."
      },
      {
        "name": "Async/Await Pattern",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "All async operations use async/await. Top-level main() function with .catch() for entry point."
      },
      {
        "name": "Pagination with for-await-of",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Uses for-await-of over listBlobsFlat() but collects ALL blobs into an array (blobs.push) before returning, violating the no-array-accumulation requirement."
      },
      {
        "name": "LRO Pattern (beginXxx + pollUntilDone)",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "No long-running operations are involved in this blob storage scenario (upload, download, list, delete are all synchronous REST calls). Criterion is not applicable and correctly not misapplied."
      },
      {
        "name": "RestError Exception Handling",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "No RestError import or catch anywhere in the codebase. No statusCode inspection for error-specific handling (e.g., 404, 409)."
      },
      {
        "name": "No Deprecated Packages",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "All packages are current @azure/* track. No deprecated azure-storage, ms-rest, or legacy packages."
      },
      {
        "name": "Logging via @azure/logger",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Imports setLogLevel from @azure/logger and calls it with a configurable log level from environment variables."
      },
      {
        "name": "package.json with Correct Dependencies",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Valid package.json with @azure/identity, @azure/logger, @azure/storage-blob. Includes tsconfig.json, @types/node, and typescript in devDependencies."
      },
      {
        "name": "Custom retry policy via StorageRetryOptions",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Configures retryOptions with StorageRetryPolicyType.EXPONENTIAL, maxTries, retryDelayInMs, and maxRetryDelayInMs — all configurable via env vars."
      },
      {
        "name": "SDK logging via @azure/logger setLogLevel()",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Calls setLogLevel() from @azure/logger with a configurable level parsed from AZURE_SDK_LOG_LEVEL env var."
      },
      {
        "name": "Blob lease acquisition before overwrite using BlobLeaseClient",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Acquires lease via blockBlobClient.getBlobLeaseClient().acquireLease() before overwriting, and releases in finally block."
      },
      {
        "name": "Uses BlockBlobClient.uploadStream() for large file streaming",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses blockBlobClient.uploadStream(fileStream, bufferSize, concurrency, options) with a createReadStream file handle."
      },
      {
        "name": "Sets blob index tags on upload via tags property",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Passes tags in the uploadStream options object: { tags: options.tags }."
      },
      {
        "name": "Downloads blob via readableStreamBody",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Checks response.readableStreamBody and reads it via async iteration in streamToBuffer()."
      },
      {
        "name": "Lists blobs using for await...of over listBlobsFlat()",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses for await (const blob of this.containerClient.listBlobsFlat()) for async iteration."
      },
      {
        "name": "Handles lease conflict errors (409 status code)",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "No error handling for 409 Conflict/lease errors. acquireLease() call has no try/catch with RestError statusCode check."
      },
      {
        "name": "Handles blob not found errors (404 status code)",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "No error handling for 404 Not Found on download or delete operations."
      },
      {
        "name": "NOT using uploadData()/upload() with full buffer",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Correctly uses uploadStream() with createReadStream, never buffers the entire file in memory."
      },
      {
        "name": "NOT using connection strings or account keys",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses ManagedIdentityCredential with endpoint URL. No connection strings or keys anywhere."
      },
      {
        "name": "NOT collecting all listed blobs into an array before processing",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "listBlobs() pushes every blob into an array and returns it. This defeats the purpose of async iteration by accumulating all results in memory."
      }
    ]
  },
  "overall_score": 21,
